## 2.2 Synthesis of core–shelled ZIF-67@SiO\(_2\) nanoparticles
\(0.2\,\mathrm{~g~}\) ZIF-67 was added to the mixed solution of \(100~\mathrm{~mL}\) methanol/deionized water \((1/1,\mathrm{v/v})\) for pretreatment, and the preZIF-67 powder was obtained by centrifugation \((8000\;\mathrm{rpm},6\;\mathrm{min})\) . The pre-ZIF-67 was ultrasonically dispersed into \(100~\mathrm{~mL}\) methanol/deionized water \((1/1,\ \ \mathrm{v/v})\) mixed solution. Then \(1\;\mathrm{mol}{\cdot}\mathrm{L}^{-1}\) NaOH aqueous solution was added to the above solution and adjusted the \(\mathrm{pH}\) to 9–10. \(0.1\ \mathrm{~g~}\) hexadecyl trimethyl ammonium bromide (CTAB) was added to the above solution, stirred for \(0.5\;\mathrm{h},\) added \(0.5\;\mathrm{g}\) tetraethyl orthosilicate (TEOS), and stirred for \(0.5\,\mathrm{h}\) . After \(15\;\mathrm{min}\) , the solution was washed with water and ethanol three times. Finally, the core–shelled ZIF-67@SiO\(_2\) nanostructures were obtained through a dry process in a vacuum at \(40\,^{\circ}\!C.\) The detailed preparation of ZIF-67 is provided in Section S2 in the ESM.
## 2.3 APTES surface-functionalized ZIF-67@SiO\(_2\) (ZIF-67@SiO\(_2\)-A)
\(0.05\,\mathrm{~g~}\) ZIF-67@SiO\(_2\) and \(0.25\,\mathrm{~g~}\) APTES were added to \(50\,\mathrm{~mL}\) ethanol/deionized water \((3/1,\ \mathrm{v/v})\) mixed solution, stirred to dissolve, and reacted for \(1\,\mathrm{~h~}\) . Next, the solution was centrifugally washed with deionized water for 3 times and then dried at \(60\ \ ^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) for \(12\ \mathrm{~h~}\) to obtain APTES modified ZIF-67@SiO\(_2\) (ZIF-67@SiO\(_2\)-A).
## 2.4 Synthesis of ZIF-67@SiO\(_2\)-A/PAM hydrogel
2.4 Synthesis of ZIF-67@SiO\(_2\)-A/PAM hydrogelAcrylamide (AM, 2.3 g), N,N'-methylenebisacrylamide (MBA, 0.03 g), and ammonium persulfate (APS, 0.15 g) were dissolved in 20 mL deionized water and stirred at 25 °C for 0.5 h, then ZIF-67@SiO\(_2\)-A (0.1 g) was put and evenly dispersed by ultrasonic. The 0.2 mL 25% GA solution was put into the above solution and stirred continuously for 0.5 h. The mixture was poured into the petri dish to crosslink for 3 h to obtain ZIF-67@SiO\(_2\)-A/PAM hydrogel. The PAM hydrogel was prepared by the same method.
